2	 * Scoped to this atom's own contract per testing.md: given href/no href, does it render the
3	 * right element type; does the href branch carry aria-checked/tabIndex tracking
4	 * isSelected/isFocusable (the href-absent branch is a plain inert span with no interactive
5	 * semantics); does the passed
6	 * imageUrl reach the DOM as the swatch's background-image fill; and — the regression guard —
7	 * does the swatch box's background-colour stay pinned to the recipe's own token declaration
8	 * regardless of the colour `name`, rather than picking up a raw CSS-colour-keyword the way base
9	 * SFCC's own `renderDefaultVariationAttribute` does (`backgroundColor={name.toLowerCase()}`) —
10	 * see index.tsx's own comment for the three reasons this atom deliberately does not replicate
11	 * that.
12	 *
13	 * Every render needs three wrappers, not just the router:
14	 *   - `ChakraProvider theme={theme}` (the real theme, not Chakra's default) — without it,
15	 *     `useMultiStyleConfig('ZimmColourSwatch', ...)` resolves against a theme with no such key
16	 *     registered and silently returns `{}` for both parts, which would make every assertion below
17	 *     pass vacuously against an unstyled node rather than against this recipe. Same reasoning as
18	 *     zimmProductMeta/index.test.tsx's own "resolves its recipe under a ChakraProvider" test.
19	 *   - `MemoryRouter` — this atom can render a react-router `Link`, which throws outside one.
20	 *   - `ZimmTokensGlobal` — without a `:root` definition for the `--zimm-*` variables the recipe
21	 *     references, a resolved-value assertion has nothing to distinguish "correct" from
22	 *     "regressed" (see the regression-guard test below).
23	 *
24	 * `getComputedStyle`, not `element.style`: Chakra resolves `__css` through Emotion, which applies
25	 * a generated class rather than an inline `style` attribute, so the inline `style` property never
26	 * reflects the resolved value — matching how every other Chakra-styles assertion in this codebase
27	 * reads a resolved value (zimmProductMeta/index.test.tsx, zimmProductPrice/index.test.tsx,
28	 * theme/index.test.tsx).
29	 *
30	 * One further, load-bearing wrinkle specific to a `var(--zimm-*)`-driven recipe (as opposed to a
31	 * bare Chakra-scale key, which those other files' assertions read): confirmed directly against
32	 * this file, jsdom's `getComputedStyle` does not substitute a custom property's value — it
33	 * echoes back the literal declaration text (`"var(--zimm-color-bg-02)"`), never the
34	 * resolved hex/rgb. That is actually what makes the regression guard below simple rather than
35	 * impossible: it asserts on that literal, unsubstituted declaration string, which is exactly
36	 * "which value authored this" — variable reference vs. some other literal. A real browser (Chrome
37	 * driving the Storybook `play` in index.stories.tsx) does perform the substitution; this file
38	 * doesn't need it to, because the literal declaration is the more direct thing to assert on.
39	 *
40	 * No ZimmIcon anywhere in this component, so no need for the ZimmIcon-throws-under-Vitest mock
41	 * documented in testing.md.
